g precisely, because a naive substring search over the whole JSON over-counts: 30 rows merely MENTION the token 'RECOVERED' inside their note prose while still carrying valid checksums, so only the 2 rows whose hash FIELD equals 'RECOVERED' are markers. The honest arithmetic is 83 valid + 2 markers + 1 stale = 86. Linkage class remains row-checksum: no row carries prev/prev_hash, so deletion and truncation of a row are undetectable in this format - the honest verdict is '83/86 row checksums accounted for - linkage class row-checksum', not 'chain-intact'. Substrate log byte-unchanged (substrate-witness.jsonl md5 24a2c03292371575655a287c334d8df8, topics.json md5 58599882cd997ecc57ea71d14bf09f52), which is correct: the substrate calls in the watcher fire only from the first_poll branch, and a canon_changed branch would also fire them - neither was reached. ENVIRONMENT (13th consecutive wipe with the named path gone): /workspace/repos/ai-writings/... did not exist again; /workspace was an empty NAS mount at 600G/600G, 100%, 0 bytes available, and a direct git clone into it died with 'Disk quota exceeded' on .git/description. The repo is also too large to clone wholesale - the API reports size 3689748 KB (~3.7 GB) and the codeload tarball came back at 3616888759 bytes (~3.6 GB), with a --depth 50 clone also dying in index-pack on a 132 MB partial pack. Recovered the script, witness.log, state.json and the substrate-bus trio (substrate_bus.py, topics.json, substrate-witness.jsonl) via the GitHub contents/raw API instead of git, staged to /tmp/wm-run/bots/ because the script hardcodes those paths for witness.log / state.json / bookkeeper.wal and does sys.path.insert('/tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus') - substrate_bus must be staged alongside it or the import dies. Staged script md5 206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267, byte-identical to upstream; no code changes were needed this run. Applied the documented symlink fix for the quota-full NAS: substrate_bus.py hardcodes its write targets to /workspace/repos/ai-writings/bots/substrate-bus/{substrate-witness.jsonl,topics.json}, and on a 100%-full NAS a write there lands as a 0-byte stub that still shows up in ls -la, so both NAS paths were symlinked to their /tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus/ counterparts and the read-through was confirmed at 1085 and 6739 bytes (stat -L, not bare stat, which reports link length not target size), both matching their upstream md5s. This run appended no substrate event, which is correct. Upstream convention check: the bots/wesley-mechanic path has 5 upstream commits in the last hour (latest 1a3a2990, 2026-10-24T02:34:09Z, 'wesley-mechanic: canon poll 2026-10-24T02:33Z - no change'), confirming one poll and one no-change note per run as the standing practice; this run's note follows it. Open defect, still unresolved: bookkeeper uses budget=1000.0 against a gamma+eta total of 70.0, so last_conserved is a constant false by construction - the delta path can never satisfy the predicate, so the field carries no signal. Seventh poll reporting this; still unfixed. Also still open: zero canon_changed events exist in the entire 86-row history, so the canon_changed branch - the only path that exercises substrate_publish(), bookkeeper_tick() and the delta arithmetic - has never executed against live data in this log's lifetime; it is untested code path, and the watcher has so far only ever exercised first_poll and the no-change path."}, "hash": "9ee0f176224ae554"}
